## CHECKLISTS & GATES

**Anti-Slop Review Gate (block merge until all pass):**
- [ ] I understand every line; nothing was accepted blindly.
- [ ] No unrequested features / no code no one asked for.
- [ ] No new dependency, abstraction, or file that isn't earning its keep.
- [ ] Duplication detector clean (no new 5+ line clones).
- [ ] Complexity / lint / dead-code sensors green.
- [ ] Defensive-coding amplification check: no gratuitous fallbacks/tolerant readers.
- [ ] Diff is small enough to review honestly (else split it).

**"Is This Abstraction Earning Its Keep?" Gate:**
- [ ] Used in ≥2 genuinely different places (not speculative)?
- [ ] Does it reduce total comprehension load, or just move it around?
- [ ] Would a newcomer understand the code faster with or without it?
- [ ] If premature → inline it now; abstract later when the third real case appears.

**WIP / Backpressure Gate:**
- [ ] ≤2–3 agent tasks in flight?
- [ ] Review queue below capacity (else shed or finish before starting new)?
- [ ] Token/turn budgets set on any autonomous run?
- [ ] Circuit-breaker / retry cap defined for this loop?

